      "created_at": "2013-12-14T13:27:29.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ameena\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ameena/48/1907_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ameena:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The discard for redirection via the amulet happens right at the moment when Nightmist would be about to take damage, so you'd go \"Right, I'm gonna hit myself\", then choose to discard two to redirect it to something else,  then  continue once that was resolved and, in this case, finish off the \"Investigate\" power by drawing two cards :). Note also that as the two parts of Investigate are listed separately (there isn't an \"If you do…\" phrase at the start of the second part), you don't have to have dealt or taken damage in order to draw cards - if you're immune to damage or have been whacked by something like Ensnaring Brambles or Ethereal Bonds and can't deal any, that's fine - you basically get to draw two cards for free :).</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Argh, I was afraid the timing was not going to work in my favor. &nbsp;The whole reason I asked was because the \"pay at the end\" scenario seemed wrong even though I really wanted it to be correct. &nbsp;It would give me a lot more flexibility in managing my hand. &nbsp;Ah well, thanks for the input.</p>",
